# GCSE Exam Question Trainer Pack

## Create

- `types/examTrainer.ts`
- `data/examTrainerQuestionBank.ts`
- `services/examTrainerService.ts`
- `components/exam-trainer/ExamQuestionTrainer.tsx`
- `app/exam-trainer/page.tsx`

## Open

After starting the app, visit:

```text
http://localhost:3000/exam-trainer
```

## Optional sidebar link

Add this item to the student sidebar links:

```ts
{
  href: "/exam-trainer",
  label: "Exam Trainer",
  icon: "🧪",
},
```

## Existing API dependency

Written-response marking uses:

```text
/api/ai/mark-lesson-question
```

This is the same endpoint used by the interactive lesson exam-question step.
Objective and exact-answer questions are marked locally.

## Current scope

This pack provides:

- topic and difficulty selection;
- generated mixed-question sessions;
- timed exams;
- multiple-choice and written-response support;
- automatic and AI marking;
- total score and estimated grade;
- topic performance;
- examiner feedback;
- mark schemes and improved answers.

Firestore persistence, attempt history and teacher analytics should be added in
the next integration pack after the user flow has been tested.

## Format and build

```powershell
npx prettier --write `
  ".\types\examTrainer.ts" `
  ".\data\examTrainerQuestionBank.ts" `
  ".\services\examTrainerService.ts" `
  ".\components\exam-trainer\ExamQuestionTrainer.tsx" `
  ".\app\exam-trainer\page.tsx"

Remove-Item -Recurse -Force ".next" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
npm run build
```

# Exam Trainer Persistence Pack

## Create

- `services/examTrainerAttemptService.ts`
- `services/examTrainerAnalyticsService.ts`
- `services/examTrainerAdaptiveEvidenceService.ts`
- `components/exam-trainer/ExamTrainerHistory.tsx`
- `app/exam-trainer/history/page.tsx`

## Replace

- `types/examTrainer.ts`
- `components/exam-trainer/ExamQuestionTrainer.tsx`

## Supporting files

- `firebase/firestore-rules-exam-trainer-snippet.txt`
- `firebase/firestore-indexes-exam-trainer.json`
- `integration/adaptive-learning-integration.txt`
- `integration/dashboard-integration.txt`
- `EXAM-MODE-INTEGRITY-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Features

- creates a Firestore attempt before an exam begins;
- autosaves answers, question position and remaining time;
- discovers and resumes an unfinished attempt;
- saves submitted examiner reports;
- prevents a submitted attempt from being resumed;
- writes topic-level result evidence beneath the user profile;
- provides student exam history;
- provides dashboard summary analytics;
- provides an Adaptive Learning evidence adapter.

## Sidebar link

Add beside Exam Trainer:

```tsx
{
  href: "/exam-trainer/history",
  label: "Exam History",
  icon: "📈",
},
```

## Firestore rules

Merge the rule blocks from:

```text
firebase/firestore-rules-exam-trainer-snippet.txt
```

into your existing rules. Do not replace all current rules with the snippet.

## Firestore indexes

The two queries use compound indexes. Either:

1. deploy the supplied index definitions after merging them with your existing
   `firestore.indexes.json`; or
2. run the page once and follow the Firebase console index-creation link.

## Adaptive Learning

Follow:

```text
integration/adaptive-learning-integration.txt
```

This is deliberately provided as a small integration instruction because your
Adaptive Learning service already contains several project-specific evidence
sources that must be preserved.

## Format and build

```powershell
npx prettier --write `
  ".\types\examTrainer.ts" `
  ".\services\examTrainerAttemptService.ts" `
  ".\services\examTrainerAnalyticsService.ts" `
  ".\services\examTrainerAdaptiveEvidenceService.ts" `
  ".\components\exam-trainer\ExamQuestionTrainer.tsx" `
  ".\components\exam-trainer\ExamTrainerHistory.tsx" `
  ".\app\exam-trainer\history\page.tsx"

Remove-Item -Recurse -Force ".next" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
npm run build
```

## Test order

1. Start an exam and answer two questions.
2. Refresh the browser.
3. Confirm the unfinished-attempt card appears.
4. Resume and confirm the answers and timer remain.
5. Submit the paper.
6. Open `/exam-trainer/history`.
7. Confirm the result appears once.
8. Refresh and confirm it is still present.
9. Complete the Adaptive Learning integration.
10. Confirm exam topic scores affect mastery recommendations.

